%[text] %[text:anchor:T_BB73E10C] # Edge Detection - Applied
%[text] [⇦ Main Menu](file:../../MainMenu.m)
%[text] This script introduces gradient-based edge detection and applies the Canny method to extract accurate object boundaries in computer vision.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Image of a set of colorful gears before and after edge detection.](text:image:7158)
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_51183E7B] **Before you get started:**
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF646A47] This live script is intended to be used with the code hidden. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Hide Code**.  Alternately, select **Hide Code** using the icon ![live script code hidden icon](text:image:4c13) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![Lightbulb mark](text:image:8eb6) Although the code is hidden, some interactivity requires familiarity with MATLAB. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2 hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8F8A032D] ![Warning symbol](text:image:62d9)   For an optimal experience, follow the instructions and steps in the given sequence. Proceed to a new section only after completing the preceding one. Some sections depend on variables created in prior sections and will generate errors if run out of order.
%[text] The ![Try this icon](text:image:9fa9)  and  ![Exercise icon](text:image:47c4) icons refer to two different types of interactive activities that you will find in this script. The ![Try this icon](text:image:6b16)  usually indicates an interaction where you will explore the visualization of some concept introduced in this script. The ![Exercise icon](text:image:8095) interactions are designed to challenge your understanding of those concepts and may be used for grading and completion checks by your professor.
